Given the following four propositions:
① If for every $x \in \mathbb{R}$, $f(x-1) = f(x+1)$ holds, then the graph of the function $f(x)$ is symmetric about the line $x=1$;
② If the function $f(x)$ is an odd function, then the graph of $f(x-1)$ is symmetric about the point $(1,0)$;
③ If $f(x+1) + f(1-x) = 0$ always holds, then the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric about the point $(1,0)$;
④ The graph of $y=f(x-1)$ is symmetric to the graph of $y=f(1-x)$ about the y-axis.
Among these propositions, the correct ones are ( )
