Given the equation $\left(5a+3b\right)^{2}=\left(5a-3b\right)^{2}+A$, we need to find the value of $A$. 

Starting from the given equation:
\begin{align*}
\left(5a+3b\right)^{2} &= \left(5a-3b\right)^{2}+A \\
\therefore A &= \left(5a+3b\right)^{2}-\left(5a-3b\right)^{2}
\end{align*}

Expanding both squares:
\begin{align*}
A &= (25a^2 + 30ab + 9b^2) - (25a^2 - 30ab + 9b^2) \\
&= 25a^2 + 30ab + 9b^2 - 25a^2 + 30ab - 9b^2 \\
&= 60ab
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $A$ is $60ab$. Hence, the correct answer is $\boxed{B}$.

