s:
Since $f(x)$ is any function defined on $\mathbb{R}$,
Let $F(x) = f(x)f(-x)$, then $F(-x) = f(-x)f[-(-x)] = f(x)f(-x) = F(x)$, so it is an even function;
Let $G(x) = f(x)|f(-x)|$, then $G(-x) = f(-x)|f[-(-x)]| = f(-x)|f(x)|$, this function is not an even function;
Let $H(x) = f(x) - f(-x)$, then $H(-x) = f(-x) - f[-(-x)] = -[f(x) - f(-x)]$, this function is not an even function;
Let $T(x) = f(x) + f(-x)$, then $T(-x) = f(-x) + f[-(-x)] = f(x) + f(-x)$, so it is an even function.
Therefore, ① and ④ are even functions.
Hence, the correct choice is $\boxed{D}$.

